id: pm-jev-ygvl
title: Explain typed decisions by bounded evidence removal
description: Measure typed decision sensitivity with bounded leave-one-field-out comparisons and opaque evidence digests; preserve existing typed questions and exemplars.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-22T16:06:12.787Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T16:19:57.887Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Removing unrelated fields leaves stable decisions; Call limits are enforced, including failed attempts and disabled transport retries; Explanation receipts disclose uncertainty and every omitted comparison; Typed SDK and CLI produce compact TOON/JSON with typed refusals and remedies, without git; Validate read-only public tracker copy and pass npm plus Bun CI release gates"
parent: pm-jev-0w3q
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T16:06:39.287Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: searched current CLI command/SDK surfaces and pm-context, pm-rl, and pm-jev sources and READMEs for counterfactual, leave-one-field-out, and decision sensitivity; no implementing feature found. Existing pm-jev typed Questions, SystemOneResult, projection, answer validation, and endpoint privacy boundary remain the model interface. pm-context owns evidence packing; pm-rl owns training/evaluation. This feature only measures bounded decision sensitivity and emits opaque receipts, never narrative rationale or tracker mutations. Plan: baseline plus sequential explicit field removals, hard network-call budget with retries disabled, one total deadline, redacted failure/omission receipts, uncertainty disclosure, non-git tests and public-copy validation. CLI registry currently reports 2026.10.22; tracker writes retain the repository-pinned 2026.10.17 SDK."
  "2026-10-22T16:13:40.217Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explainDecision SDK and jev explain command using host SDK item reads, existing projection, existing typed Questions parser/answer validator, official TypeSafe transport and endpoint privacy guard. Calls are sequential, retries disabled, baseline counted, one shared deadline; successes survive interruption and every skipped field is disclosed. Evidence uses fresh per-run HMAC-SHA256 digests. Tests exercise a real non-git SDK tracker and real HTTP transport plus the built extension through the actual host parser in TOON/JSON with an empty PATH. Targeted checks exposed and fixed the host exit-code contract (success omits exit_code) and empty explicit budget handling (must refuse instead of using the SDK option reader default). Public-copy validation is running against verified public committed pm-lint data with immutable copied files and before/after hashes."
  "2026-10-22T16:15:01.591Z",codex-agent,"Validation: targeted counterfactual suite 8 passed, 0 failed/skipped. c8 over counterfactual.ts and counterfactual-command.ts measured 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, zero-duplication and public-provenance checks pass at unchanged thresholds. Revert proof: removing only the field-deletion behavior makes the unrelated/relevant-field regression fail (0 pass, 1 fail); restoring it and disabling only the call-budget guard makes the budget regression fail (0 pass, 1 fail). Both behaviors restored afterward. Public real-data validation: verified unbraind/pm-lint commit 7420b83854f22498fa564cf41bc4d298e8e593f4; 13 tracker items, 6 sampled, 32 authoritative files hash-verified unchanged, 24 SDK calls plus 2 CLI calls using tev1:4b; 18 completed comparisons, 13 stable and 5 changed, 2 explicitly budget-omitted CLI comparisons; compact SDK JSON 1421..1432 bytes. All 3 sampled empty-tag removals were stable; 5 of 6 total tag removals were stable. This is single-sample sensitivity, not accuracy, causal attribution or model-noise certification. No full release gate was run on the saturated host; npm and Bun full gates will run in CI."
  "2026-10-22T16:15:55.566Z",codex-agent,"Host health boundary: ordinary strict health reproduces the existing ambient global-extension skew tracked by pm-jev-v2la. With isolated HOME and global Git configuration disabled, strict health passes, including history integrity. No dependency pins, global installations or tracker history were rewritten. Linked test execution through pm test completed 8 passed with no skipped tests; test-result tracking is disabled by repository policy, so this comment records the measured result without changing that policy."
  "2026-10-22T16:18:12.802Z",codex-agent,"Implementation commit 34aa4c8 is published as ready-for-review PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/42. CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/actions/runs/39812672937 is running the full npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26; clean-checkout strict tracker health and generated-dist consistency have already passed both jobs. Automated reviews are currently unavailable or skipped (review budget/trial/automatic-review eligibility); these statuses are not review approval. No reviewers were mentioned and no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-22T16:19:56.026Z",codex-agent,"Implementation CI passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/actions/runs/39812672937 at commit 34aa4c82c0c00a26031ce4d8cf6a868e8704079b. Node 22 npm, Node 22 Bun, Node 26 npm and Node 26 Bun each ran release:check: 304 tests passed, 0 failed/cancelled/skipped; all 27 source files reported, 100% statements/branches/functions/lines at unchanged thresholds. Docstrings: 711 documented declarations; duplication: 0% across 71 sources. Both clean-checkout health and dist consistency passed; CodeQL also passed. Final handoff changes only tracker receipt/claim metadata and will rerun CI; PR 42 will retain the final exact-head run URL and counts. No known feature blockers; limitations remain single-sample noise/interactions and unavailable independent automated review. Existing ambient extension SDK issue pm-jev-v2la remains open. Implementation item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
